# Every supply with nowhere to put its excess that states all its unserved shares, beside what
# its own numbers say went unserved. One row per examined layer, `violates` where the exposure
# exceeds what anybody admits.
#
# A measure with no instrument behind it
#   This is the one place this model measures something with no instrument behind it. Nobody
#   filed the exposure; it is the ceiling the filer's own demand and nameplate imply: the largest
#   demand against the smallest supply. What could have gone unserved is at most what the buffer
#   can absorb plus what they admit went unserved, and the buffer here absorbs nothing by their
#   own measurement. So the whole exposure has to be accounted for in the holder rows.
#
# `absorbable` is read, never assumed
#   It is a sum across the whole buffer row and it is zero by construction of this population,
#   where a literal `0` in the sentence below would be a claim about the capacity column alone.
#
# Evaluated at the high corner, on purpose
#   The two sides of a transition fit are anti-correlated (the week demand ran highest is not the
#   week supply ran lowest), so anything summed across the demand range reports a week that never
#   happened.
#
# An unstated unserved share suspends the inequality
#   Those layers are absent rather than passing. Inheriting a neighbouring rule's `exposure > 0`
#   filter instead is a different population, so its count is not a count of what this rule
#   checks.
#
# Unserved shares in another unit are not compared
#   A share quoted in a unit other than the layer's is not a smaller share; it is not a share of
#   this remainder at all, and summing it against the exposure is a comparison with no answer.
#   arithmetic/exposure_bounded.sqlc calls those layers `not comparable`, and this rule leaves them
#   out rather than judging them. Proof: `src/proofs/README.md`, entry `exposure_bound`.
#
# The unserved total is inner-joined
#   An outer join here invents rows. `coalesce(u.unserved, 0)` gives a layer with no unserved
#   holder a zero nobody filed, so such layers enter the examined set. They all read
#   `exposure = 0`, so `0 > 0 + 1e-9` is false and the rule passes on every one of them without
#   being able to fire. arithmetic/exposure_bounded.sqlc, the site this rule guards, inner-joins;
#   a guard and its site disagreeing about their population is the guard's defect, and
#   reports/coverage.sqlc would count the difference as coverage.
-- every slack on the layer accounted for and empty, against entries/unserved_totals.sqlc.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT e.filing, e.layer,
           e.exposure > e.unserved + 1e-9 AS violates,
           format('exposure %s, absorbable %s, unserved %s',
                  e.exposure, e.absorbable, e.unserved) AS detail
    FROM (
        SELECT x.filing, x.layer, x.exposure, x.absorbable, u.unserved_high AS unserved
        FROM      (
            :compose(layers/unabsorbed_exposure.sqlc)
        ) x
        JOIN      (
            :compose(entries/unserved_totals.sqlc)
        ) u USING (filing, layer)
        WHERE u.unstated = 0
          AND u.share_units = ARRAY[x.unit]
    ) e
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'exposure_unaccounted'
